Available Tools
===============

- Tool Name: `object_detection_image`
  Description: Detect/localize visible objects or classes; returns JSON boxes only. Not for enhancement, upscaling, restoration, lighting, face, or color edits.
  Args:
    {
      "text_prompt": {"type": "string", "description": "Objects/classes to detect, e.g. 'cat' or 'person . dog'. Use 'object' if unspecified."},
      "box_threshold": {"type": "number", "description": "Box confidence threshold. Default 0.3."},
      "text_threshold": {"type": "number", "description": "Text matching threshold. Default 0.25."}
    }
  Output Schema:
    {
      "observation": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "image_size": {"description": "Input image size."},
          "detections_count": {"type": "integer", "description": "Detection count."},
          "predictions": {"type": "array", "description": "Detected boxes and metadata."}
        }
      }
    }
  Example:
    {
      "tool_name": "object_detection_image",
      "args": {"text_prompt": "person . backpack . bench", "box_threshold": 0.3, "text_threshold": 0.25}
    }

- Tool Name: `low_light_enhance`
  Description: Brighten low-light or underexposed images. Not for detection, upscaling, denoise, deblur, face, or color edits.
  Args:
    {}
  Output Schema:
    {
      "observation": {"type": "string", "description": "Low-light image brightening completed."}
    }
  Example:
    {
      "tool_name": "low_light_enhance",
      "args": {}
    }

- Tool Name: `zoom_in_image`
  Description: Crop/enlarge a detected region for detail, text, or small objects. Requires an exact prior object_detection_image box; never guess coordinates.
  Args:
    {
      "box": {"type": "array", "description": "Pixel box [x_min, y_min, x_max, y_max] copied from observation.predictions[].box."},
      "padding_ratio": {"type": "number", "description": "Box padding ratio. Default 0.2."},
      "min_output_size": {"type": "integer", "description": "Minimum long side after resize. Default 768."}
    }
  Output Schema:
    {
      "observation": {"type": "string", "description": "Image crop and zoom-in enlargement completed."}
    }
  Example:
    {
      "tool_name": "zoom_in_image",
      "args": {"box": [120, 80, 310, 460], "padding_ratio": 0.2, "min_output_size": 768}
    }

- Tool Name: `rotate_image`
  Description: Rotate/straighten when requested, or only when VQA needs it and direction is clear. Not for guessed orientation or non-rotation tasks.
  Args:
    {
      "angle": {"type": "number", "description": "Rotation angle in degrees."},
      "direction": {"type": "string", "enum": ["clockwise", "counterclockwise"], "description": "Rotation direction. Default clockwise."},
      "expand": {"type": "boolean", "description": "Expand canvas after rotation. Default true."},
      "fill_color": {"type": "string", "description": "Corner fill color. Default white or transparent."}
    }
  Output Schema:
    {
      "observation": {"type": "string", "description": "Rotation completion message; not orientation verification."}
    }
  Example:
    {
      "tool_name": "rotate_image",
      "args": {"angle": 90, "direction": "clockwise", "expand": true}
    }

- Tool Name: `nafnet_image_restoration`
  Description: Denoise/deblur noisy or blurred images when requested. Not for ordinary VQA, detection, upscaling, lighting, face, or color edits.
  Args:
    {
      "mode": {"type": "string", "enum": ["denoise", "deblur"], "description": "Restoration mode."}
    }
  Output Schema:
    {
      "observation": {"type": "string", "description": "Denoise/deblur completion message."}
    }
  Example:
    {
      "tool_name": "nafnet_image_restoration",
      "args": {"mode": "denoise"}
    }

- Tool Name: `super_resolution_image`
  Description: Upscale low-resolution or pixelated images. Not for lighting, deblur, denoise, face, detection, or color edits.
  Args:
    {
      "bs": {"type": "integer", "description": "Batch size. Default 1."}
    }
  Output Schema:
    {
      "observation": {"type": "string", "description": "Image super-resolution upscaling completed."}
    }
  Example:
    {
      "tool_name": "super_resolution_image",
      "args": {"bs": 1}
    }
